**Discussion Points:**  
- Dr. Emily Chen opened the meeting by reiterating the importance of Drug X, targeting Alzheimer's disease, currently in Phase 2 trials at the University of California, San Francisco (UCSF).  
- John Carter provided an update on the current enrollment status, noting that 85% of the 300 participants have been recruited across sites including UCSF and Mount Sinai Health System in New York.  
- Sarah Patel discussed the upcoming FDA pre-IND meeting scheduled for November 10, 2023, emphasizing the need for detailed data from the ongoing trials to support the Investigational New Drug application.  
- Dr. Mark Thompson reported preliminary efficacy results, indicating a 20% improvement in cognitive function measured by the MMSE (Mini-Mental State Examination) compared to placebo controls.  
- Lisa Reynolds raised concerns regarding quality control during the manufacturing scale-up at BioPharma’s facility in Cambridge, MA, stressing adherence to Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP).  
- David Wang outlined the production timeline, aiming for batch production of 10,000 units by Q2 2024, contingent on successful trial outcomes.  
- Rachel Kim highlighted the budgetary implications of the projected timelines, indicating potential cost overruns of 15% if the FDA approval process is delayed.  

